### Events

Use `calculatedColumnChanged` to track changes to `headerName`, `cellDataType`, `calculatedExpression` and `columnGroupShow`. Its `changes` object contains only changed properties, with their previous and new values. Cell values read in the handler already reflect the change, including in calculated columns that depend on it. Deferred Apply raises one event for all changes. Live mode raises one per applied update, with `applyDebounce` combining edits after a pause in typing. Initialisation and Grid State restoration do not raise this event.

Check `expressionValidation.valid` before saving an accepted expression. When invalid, `expressionValidation.reason` is `restrictedReference`, `customValidation`, `unknownReference` or `invalidExpression`. Validation-only updates also raise this event, with an empty `changes` object and the unchanged `expression`.

`calculatedColumnValidationStateChanged` reports changes to built-in validation status after an edit is applied, not while it is pending. Callback rejections are reported through `calculatedColumnChanged.expressionValidation` instead.

```js
const gridOptions = {
    onCalculatedColumnChanged: event => {
        const { headerName, cellDataType, calculatedExpression } = event.changes;
        if (headerName) {
            console.log('Title:', headerName.oldValue, headerName.newValue);
        }
        if (cellDataType) {
            console.log('Type:', cellDataType.oldValue, cellDataType.newValue);
        }
        if (calculatedExpression && event.expressionValidation.valid) {
            console.log('Expression:', calculatedExpression.oldValue, calculatedExpression.newValue);
        }
    },
};
```

{% note %}
Live expressions can be incomplete or invalid. Recognised references use stored `colId` values, such as `[revenue]`; references the dialog cannot resolve remain as typed, so they can still contain header names.

`expressionValidation` is a snapshot of syntax, direct reference resolution and saved dialog errors, not row-specific evaluation results. To persist rejected expressions with their blocked status, save [Grid State](./grid-state/); saving only the expression text does not retain that status.
{% /note %}

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-events/events.json" section="calculatedColumns" names=["calculatedColumnCreated", "calculatedColumnChanged", "calculatedColumnRemoved", "calculatedColumnValidationStateChanged"] /%}
